# Production apply order of the out-of-tree kernel patches (Linux 6.18.63).
# Buildroot does NOT read this file: BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_PATCH in
# tp2bmc/configs/tp2bmc_defconfig lists the same directories in the same
# order, and each directory's *.patch files are applied in name order.
#
# Series taken from excavador-turing/BMC-Firmware#79 (Daniel Steinhauf,
# @danste22), hardware LAG included: net-dsa/0014 to 0016 offload a bond onto
# the switch's trunk hardware. net-dsa/0017 is not LAG code, it fixes the FDB
# keying of the bridge offload in 0009 (see the patch); it comes after the LAG
# patches because that is the order #79 built and tested.
generic/i2c/0001-i2c-mv64xxx-Clear-bus-errors-before-transfer.patch
generic/pwm/0001-dt-bindings-pwm-Add-binding-for-Allwinner-D1-T113-S3.patch
generic/pwm/0002-pwm-Add-Allwinner-s-D1-T113-S3-R329-SoCs-PWM-support.patch
generic/pwm/0003-riscv-dts-allwinner-d1-Add-pwm-node.patch
net-dsa/0001-net-dsa-tag_rtl8_4-update-format-description.patch
net-dsa/0002-net-dsa-tag_rtl8_4-set-KEEP-flag.patch
net-dsa/0003-net-dsa-realtek-rtl8365mb-use-ERR_PTR.patch
net-dsa/0004-net-dsa-realtek-rtl8365mb-reject-unsupported-topolog.patch
net-dsa/0005-net-dsa-realtek-rtl8365mb-use-dsa-helpers-for-port-i.patch
net-dsa/0006-net-dsa-realtek-rtl8365mb-prepare-for-multiple-sourc.patch
net-dsa/0007-net-dsa-realtek-rtl8365mb-add-table-lookup-interface.patch
net-dsa/0008-net-dsa-realtek-rtl8365mb-add-VLAN-support.patch
net-dsa/0009-net-dsa-realtek-rtl8365mb-add-FDB-support.patch
net-dsa/0010-net-dsa-realtek-rtl8365mb-add-port_bridge_-join-leav.patch
net-dsa/0011-net-dsa-realtek-rtl8365mb-add-bridge-port-flags.patch
net-dsa/0012-net-dsa-realtek-rtl8365mb-provide-field_get-on-v6.18.patch
